WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
If your prep is SuTab, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:03.840
it.

3
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.170
Just follow along step by step. Your SuTab kit includes two bottles of 12

4
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:09.920
tablets each

5
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.680
and a measured container. Start your first dose between 6 and 7 PM the night

6
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.720
before your procedure.

7
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.050
Open your first bottle of 12 tablets. Fill the provided container with 16

8
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:22.640
ounces of

9
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.170
water up to the fill line. Swallow one tablet every 2 minutes with a sip of

10
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:27.840
water,

11
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.750
finishing all 12 tablets over about 15 to 20 minutes. Take your time and go at

12
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.760
a steady pace.

13
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.560
About 1 hour after your last tablet, fill the container again with 16 ounces

14
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:39.200
of water

15
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.950
and drink the entire amount slowly over 30 minutes. Then, about 30 minutes

16
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.720
after finishing

17
00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:49.220
that container, fill it one more time with 16 ounces of water and drink the

18
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:49.600
entire amount

19
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.570
over 30 minutes. That completes your first dose. 7 hours prior to your

20
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:55.440
procedure,

21
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.940
repeat the exact same three steps using your second bottle of 12 tablets. One

22
00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:00.240
tablet every

23
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.770
2 minutes with water, then 16 ounces of water one hour later, then 16 ounces

24
00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:05.760
of water 30 minutes

25
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.390
after that. This part is really important. You must drink all of the prep

26
00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.640
solution as directed,

27
00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.880
even if you're already passing clear liquid. I know it can feel like enough,

28
00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.440
but finishing the

29
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.580
entire dose is what gives us the clearest view during your procedure. If the

30
00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:20.480
prep isn't completed

31
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.010
as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither of us wants that. Between

32
00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.000
doses, keep drinking

33
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.590
clear liquids to stay hydrated. It will help you feel better and help the prep

34
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:30.240
do its job.

35
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.300
Do not drink anything at all within 4 hours of your procedure, including

36
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:35.760
water,

37
00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.320
unless it is a small sip to take a medication. Your procedure may be canceled

38
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.120
or rescheduled

39
00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.480
if this is not followed. If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips

40
00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:46.560
to the bathroom,

41
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.240
applying a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

42
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:56.650
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

43
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:57.120
hydrated.

44
00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:02.260
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

45
00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.760
to help.
